From 5993ed51aa6389f7b2c8d9a3ff3b36fff2b72460 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 07:53:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 286: anon resolves the fork; the mind becomes relational -
 identity unrepresentable

The anon arm answered what it was built to answer. The inversion is gone -
unknown AUC 0.302 at -2.3 sigma became 0.579 at +0.9 - so identity in the
read text was the poison, exactly as staked. But the channel does not pay:
parity with nohid at matched coverage (0.431 = 0.431), a LOSS on the lying
tape (0.410 against votes 0.462 where nohid won 0.487), and a train control
still memorised at AUC 0.997, because an anonymised sentence is still a
unique string. One genuine positive, the first of its kind: a legitimate
G_weighs_contested pass at 0.364 against random 0.268 against votes 0.121.
Structure, once the names are gone, carries something. The pre-registered
fork resolves to "drop the raw-reading channel".

Three autopsies now say one sentence from three sides: everything trainable
over an input that contains identity becomes a lookup table. Trunk frozen -
collapse stays. Capacity cut 12.8x - fit unchanged to the digit. Names folded
out - poison gone, payoff absent. And the only head that ever passed an exam
here is nine relational statistics, which transfer precisely because they
cannot name anyone. That is not a post-mortem, it is a design rule.

--mind relational builds the mind to that rule. An equivariant network over
the mention graph whose every input is an indicator or a within-example RANK:
same-value; rank of context-fp cosine; rank of shared-rare-word overlap, rare
meaning rarer than the tape's median (284's rank rule, no threshold); rank of
external corroboration; the value's share of the evidence. No text, no
fingerprint, no absolute coordinate of any kind reaches the weights, so the
lookup channel is closed by construction rather than discouraged by
regularisation. Sum/mean pools over mentions and over each candidate's
coalition make it equivariant - the same ~5k weights read 3 mentions or 300,
which is the "mind does not grow with the knowledge" invariant realised as
architecture, and the scale story in the same breath. UNKNOWN stays a row;
the answer stays the argmax; the examiners, tapes and gates do not move.

What this can express that counters cannot: two mentions with near-identical
contexts are ONE witness repeated, not two. --lie-dup K is the exam for
exactly that - the forged mention repeated K times, votes scaling linearly in
K by construction, G_survives_duplicated_lie reported alongside the verdict.

Falsifiers, before any run: the train-control AUC must FALL from ~1.0 - ranks
re-shuffle on a fresh tape, so if it stays memorised the relation graph
itself leaks identity and the class has failed its own reason to exist;
matched coverage must reach nohid's, since the nine features are derivable
from the graph; and the win, if there is one, must show on the contested
subset or the duplicated lie, the two places counting cannot go.

The trunk is never read on this arm, so a full run costs minutes, not hours.

